Ghostframe is licensed in two parts.

  Server: AGPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt)

    ghostframe-lib, ghostframe-server, and the test and benchmark crates
    built on them: ghostframe-e2e, ghostframe-bench,
    ghostframe-test-pattern.

  Everything else: MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option
  (LICENSES/MIT.txt, LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

    The wire format (ghostframe-protocol), the tailnet bridge
    (ghostframe-tsnet, ghostbridge), every client crate (ghostframe-client-*,
    ghostframe-cli), the browser client (ghostframe-web-client), the client
    shaders (shaders/), and the scripts and tools (ci/, tests/, tools/).

Each crate's Cargo.toml `license` field is the authority for that crate, and
every source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier line naming its
licence. ci/check-licenses.py checks both, and that no permissively licensed
crate depends on an AGPL one. The reasoning, and the rule for new crates, is
in AGENTS.md ("Licensing").

Some files are third-party code under their own licence, marked in the file
and listed in NOTICE (for example ghostframe-lib/src/transport/delivery_rate.rs,
Apache-2.0, from Tencent TQUIC).

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally
submit for inclusion in Ghostframe is licensed under the licence of the
part it is submitted to, as above, without any additional terms or
conditions.
